Expected outcomes on 8xH100

    Table shows bottleneck bandwidth, note in readme says max bandwidth. 
    They just mean sustained bandwidth.

    H800 is down-clocked NVLink of H100, 25GB/s per link as opposed to 50GB/s (bidir).
    In theory, peak BW between a pair of gpu is 25*18=450GB/s (H100).

    Log above tells us 
    For config: num_tokens=4096, hidden=7168, num_topk=8/256 (DeepSeek V3 MoE config)
    the comm can sustain ~330GB/s at max, effectively 330/450=73.3% of spec.

    The number above is 2X of documented. Expected since H100 BW = 2X H800


Why 24 SMs?

    On H100 GPUs, there are 132 SMs total, but for communication kernels like this, 
    they're likely using a subset to avoid saturating all GPU resources while testing the NVLink bandwidth. 
    Using 24 SMs (roughly 18% of the GPU) leaves headroom for the actual communication to be the bottleneck rather than compute.
    If you wanted to test with different SM counts, you could modify that line to:
    for i in (16, 24, 32, 48):
